After nine years of on-and-off NetHack, including seven of those years
without spoilers, I've finally ascended my first character.  Well, first
without cheating.  Long ago, I was a savescummer, but I've since repented
and am living the clean life with no temptation to regress.

Ursula started out humbly as a valkyrie, but Tyr smiled upon her as she
found two magic lamps before reaching Mine Town, turning them into two
regular oil lamps, a suit of GDSM, and some boots of speed to go with Mojo
(which she acquired on dungeon level two after only two sacrifices!) and
the ]GoP that she just FOUND in the mines.  I suddenly felt like this
character had real potential.

Ursula also found a bag of holding in one of the shops, and a luckstone at
the bottom of the mines.  She obtained her amulet of reflection in Sokoban
and, in the meantime, diligently worked towards assembling some solid armor.
Lucking out with some good, albeit generic, items, Ursula had a -12 AC by
the time she encountered the remains of Tyra, a valkyrie who'd gone before
her.

The ghost was no problem, and getting the extra bag of holding (happily,
uncursed) and a few useful wands was great.  Unfortunately, Tyra's old pet
titan Gigantes had gone a little wild, and he proved to be a bit of a
bugger.  He summoned two dragons, an umber hulk, a master lich, and a master
mind flayer right off the bat.  Ursula dealt with these things decisively
and directly.  She ran away.  Actually, she started by running down hallways
and throwing Mojo at them, except once it didn't return.  She had Sunsword
in a bag somewhere, but it didn't seem like a good idea.  Anyway, she lured
the monsters away, grabbed Mojo again, then ran away and came back later to
deal with everything.

After some searching and lots of digging, Ursula found Fort Ludios on level
19, which she cleaned out to get money for protection.  It took most of it,
too, since she was already level 12.

After getting two wraith corpses from a graveyard, Ursula was level 14 and,
I thought, ready to tackle her quest.  She had most of the resistances and
a -37 AC.  Mojo was +5 and her equipment was in good shape.  She smoked Lord
Surtur and continued on her quest.

By the time she cleared out the castle and used the /WoW, Ursula was level
15 with a -45 AC, all of the significant resistances, and a full set of
armor (except no Hawaiian shirt, but that came later).  Gehenom was almost a
letdown.

Asmodeus and Baalzebub were bribed because Ursula didn't feel like fighting
them.  Net cost: 23 gold.  Orcus killed himself with his /WoD.  Rodney was
disintegrated, Yeenoghu got summoned and killed, and Juiblex didn't even get
to engulf.  Ursula cleared the Sanctum the hard way: by killing everything.
Which was also the modus operandi all through the planes.  On the Astral
Plane, she got lucky and only had to kill Pestilence twice before going to
the right altar right away.  This valkyrie was decked out with the
equipment: all through Gehenom, she never lost more than 35hp from her max.
Although I did die once, and I don't know how.  I just noticed I wasn't
wearing my AoLS from Vlad's tower, and then the final intrinsics said I died
once.  Guess I should have paid more attention during those melees!

